{"term":"go for","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:462bc5aa500b72c251","definition":"Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see go, for.","example":"I'll go for some milk.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0733d48de0f0074783","definition":"To try for, to attempt to reach.","example":"I'll go for the world record.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b5633d533bb87316f7","definition":"To undertake (an action); to choose an option.","example":"His phone was off and I couldn't ask his permission, so I decided to just go for it.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2653bf3779b6e2529f","definition":"To attack.","example":"Careful, he'll go for your throat!","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b3a19fa76fe814caa5","definition":"To develop a strong interest in, especially in a sudden manner; to be infatuated with.","example":"Douglas: Well done on passing the test, Jen... Yes, all those clumsy attempts at seduction. Don't tell me you couldn't see through them. They were a test to find out whether you really wanted to work for me or whether you just wanted to come up here for my body.\nJen: Oh, no, no, no, no, no, not at all.\nDouglas: All right.\nJen: No, physically you're just not the sort of man I go for.\nDouglas: Yeah, thanks, Jen.\nJen: I go for the classically good-looking men: Blond, broad, and generally clean shaven.\nDouglas: Alright, yeah, enough of the jibber-jabber!","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:64adbaebbe7a983cd0","definition":"To favor, accept; to have a preference for.","example":"Management won't go for such a risky project now.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3e615adb1e1d30d9d1","definition":"To fall for (a trick)","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b1a7848a1526b69bbf","definition":"To apply equally to.","example":"Stop taking my food from the fridge! That goes for you too, Nick!","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f92b69688fa39cea8","definition":"To suffice to be used for; to serve as.","example":"It's a desk that goes for a dresser too.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:96a3e2c6aff3a2b44a","definition":"To be accepted as.","example":"The man went among men for an old man in the days of Saul.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:024d8db13065b12c83","definition":"To cost.","example":"Here in Texas, gas can go for as little as two dollars a gallon.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic","register":"idiomatic, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/go_for#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{},"wordFamily":[]}